WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.853 --> 00:00:15.473
going on?"

2
00:00:15.913 --> 00:00:16.774
someone shouted.

3
00:00:16.794 --> 00:00:19.135
"My car just stopped!"

4
00:00:19.375 --> 00:00:20.455
the mayor exclaimed.

5
00:00:21.516 --> 00:00:24.617
Several people rushed toward the mayor's car, including Mr.

6
00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:27.198
Newman. After a moment Mr.

7
00:00:27.238 --> 00:00:28.298
Newman let out a shout.

8
00:00:28.318 --> 00:00:31.860
"The car is out of gas," he announced.

9
00:00:33.036 --> 00:00:33.957
The mayor frowned.

10
00:00:34.637 --> 00:00:38.400
"You said you filled it before you dropped it off at the parking lot last night."

11
00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:40.121
"I did."

12
00:00:40.441 --> 00:00:42.002
Mr. Newman looked perplexed.

13
00:00:42.943 --> 00:00:45.665
"Maybe there's a hole in the gas tank," someone called out.

14
00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.327
More people gathered around the car.

15
00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:51.169
Henry and his friends watched from their float.

16
00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:54.051
"Uh-oh," Maggie blurted out.

17
00:00:54.071 --> 00:00:56.553
"It looks like that threat is coming true!"

18
00:00:56.573 --> 00:01:00.736
"The car was parked at the high school all night," Cole said.

19
00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:04.881
"Someone could have sneaked in and drained most of the gas.

20
00:01:06.121 --> 00:01:09.202
That way the car would stall after a few minutes."

21
00:01:10.582 --> 00:01:13.223
"And mess up the parade," Henry finished.

22
00:01:13.243 --> 00:01:16.064
"That's exactly what I was thinking.

23
00:01:16.644 --> 00:01:18.385
But who could have done that?"

24
00:01:19.485 --> 00:01:20.525
"What about Jackson?"

25
00:01:20.745 --> 00:01:21.645
Cole suggested.

26
00:01:21.665 --> 00:01:26.307
"He knew all about the parade plans because of his newspaper story.

27
00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:30.748
So he probably knew the mayor's car was parked at the high school."

28
00:01:32.036 --> 00:01:33.357
"Mr. Newman knew too."

29
00:01:34.178 --> 00:01:38.380
Maggie shot a look at the auto shop owner, who was under the car, checking the gas tank.

30
00:01:39.321 --> 00:01:41.863
"Maybe he didn't really fill the mayor's gas tank."

31
00:01:41.883 --> 00:01:43.464
"But Mr.

32
00:01:43.564 --> 00:01:47.907
Newman doesn't have a motive for ruining the parade," Henry reminded her.

33
00:01:47.927 --> 00:01:50.609
"I know someone who has a motive."

34
00:01:51.669 --> 00:01:53.110
Maggie pointed toward the shops.

35
00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.472
"We're stopped right in front of Miss Bishop's store.

36
00:01:57.393 --> 00:02:01.336
Maybe that was her plan all along—to get people to notice her store!"

37
00:02:02.676 --> 00:02:04.337
"Maybe," Cole said.

38
00:02:04.977 --> 00:02:05.717
Then he grinned.

39
00:02:05.737 --> 00:02:11.820
"But I can't imagine Miss Bishop getting her hands dirty by draining gas from a tank!"

40
00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:13.641
"Why not?"

41
00:02:13.981 --> 00:02:14.941
Maggie challenged him.

42
00:02:14.961 --> 00:02:16.902
"Because she's a woman?

43
00:02:17.342 --> 00:02:19.663
Lots of girls and women know how to drain gas."

44
00:02:20.744 --> 00:02:21.524
Cole shrugged.

45
00:02:21.864 --> 00:02:22.444
"That's true.

46
00:02:23.125 --> 00:02:25.406
I'm just not sure Miss Bishop is one of them.

47
00:02:26.426 --> 00:02:29.587
She wouldn't want to mess up her manicure."

48
00:02:30.188 --> 00:02:31.028
Henry gasped.

49
00:02:31.628 --> 00:02:32.309
"That's it!"

50
00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:34.831
"What?" Cole asked.

51
00:02:34.851 --> 00:02:36.852
"Is Miss Bishop the culprit?"

52
00:02:37.933 --> 00:02:40.635
"No, but I'm pretty sure I know who is."

53
00:02:43.117 --> 00:02:45.880
Henry peered into the watching crowd, and then smiled.

54
00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.201
"Come with me!"

55
00:02:49.362 --> 00:02:52.725
He jumped down from the float and led his friends toward Snake and his band.

56
00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:56.108
The band was watching from the sidewalk as Mr.

57
00:02:56.188 --> 00:02:58.149
Newman and others checked the mayor's car.

58
00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.132
Maggie gasped when she saw them.

59
00:03:02.056 --> 00:03:03.677
"It was Snake, wasn't it?"

60
00:03:03.977 --> 00:03:04.617
she whispered.

61
00:03:04.637 --> 00:03:05.938
"I knew it!"

62
00:03:06.978 --> 00:03:08.479
"No, it wasn't Snake."

63
00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:10.740
Henry stopped in front of the band.

64
00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.220
"Hi, guys.

65
00:03:12.781 --> 00:03:14.581
Jade, can I talk to you?"

66
00:03:14.601 --> 00:03:16.282
"What is it?"

67
00:03:16.642 --> 00:03:17.763
Jade sounded sullen.

68
00:03:18.843 --> 00:03:20.044
Henry took a deep breath.

69
00:03:20.884 --> 00:03:22.345
"You did it, didn't you?"

70
00:03:22.685 --> 00:03:23.205
he said.

71
00:03:23.225 --> 00:03:28.067
"You left that threat on the website, and you emptied the gas tank."

72
00:03:29.127 --> 00:03:30.068
Jade gasped.

73
00:03:30.848 --> 00:03:31.708
"How did you know?"

74
00:03:32.028 --> 00:03:32.749
she blurted out.

75
00:03:33.269 --> 00:03:34.389
Then she covered her mouth.

76
00:03:34.409 --> 00:03:38.470
"Um, I mean, I don't know what you're talking about!"

77
00:03:39.711 --> 00:03:42.191
Snake and the other band members looked confused.

78
00:03:42.211 --> 00:03:44.012
"What's going on?"

79
00:03:44.292 --> 00:03:45.032
Snake asked.

80
00:03:45.052 --> 00:03:48.493
"Jade, what's the Lemonade Kid talking about?"

81
00:03:49.494 --> 00:03:51.834
"Nothing," Jade muttered, glaring at Henry.

82
00:03:51.854 --> 00:03:54.515
"So Jade is our culprit?"

83
00:03:54.835 --> 00:03:55.475
Cole said.

84
00:03:55.495 --> 00:03:57.276
"How'd you know that, Henry?"

85
00:03:58.408 --> 00:04:03.290
"It was what Maggie said about girls being able to drain gas," Henry said.

86
00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:07.992
"That's when I remembered that Jade works at her father's garage.

87
00:04:09.093 --> 00:04:12.034
So she probably knows all about stuff like that.

88
00:04:13.134 --> 00:04:14.775
I also remembered that Mr.

89
00:04:14.855 --> 00:04:16.236
Newman is pretty strict.

90
00:04:17.296 --> 00:04:21.338
So I figured Jade was the band member who got grounded for being late."

91
00:04:22.318 --> 00:04:23.559
"Yeah, so what?"

92
00:04:23.839 --> 00:04:24.439
Eddie said.

93
00:04:24.459 --> 00:04:26.620
"That doesn't prove anything."

94
00:04:27.924 --> 00:04:28.725
Snake nodded.

95
00:04:28.745 --> 00:04:31.326
"It wasn't Jade's fault she got grounded.

96
00:04:32.227 --> 00:04:33.768
We talked her into staying late."

97
00:04:33.788 --> 00:04:36.350
"Okay," Henry said.

98
00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:41.373
"But I think she still felt guilty about making the band drop out of the parade.

99
00:04:42.474 --> 00:04:44.555
So she left that threat on the website.

100
00:04:45.676 --> 00:04:49.439
Then she messed with the mayor's car to try to ruin the parade."

101
00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:51.540
"I'm sorry!"

102
00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.181
Jade burst into tears.

103
00:04:53.201 --> 00:04:56.564
"I was just mad, that's all.

104
00:04:57.768 --> 00:04:59.809
I was only ten minutes late to work!

105
00:05:00.209 --> 00:05:02.590
Why does my dad have to be so strict?"

106
00:05:03.951 --> 00:05:04.951
Snake stared at her.

107
00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:06.652
"So you did this?"

108
00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:08.993
He waved a hand toward the mayor's car.

109
00:05:09.733 --> 00:05:10.893
"Not cool, Jade."

110
00:05:12.674 --> 00:05:13.114
"I know."

111
00:05:13.555 --> 00:05:14.455
Jade sniffled.

112
00:05:14.475 --> 00:05:18.276
"You've got to tell the mayor you did it," Henry said.

113
00:05:18.296 --> 00:05:21.718
"Otherwise he might blame your dad."

114
00:05:22.798 --> 00:05:23.839
Jade sniffled again.

115
00:05:23.859 --> 00:05:26.520
"Okay," she mumbled.

116
00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:28.801
"I'll go confess right now."

117
00:05:33.343 --> 00:05:37.205
Soon someone brought more gas for the mayor's car, and the parade continued.

118
00:05:41.006 --> 00:05:41.867
In the end Mrs.

119
00:05:41.927 --> 00:05:45.808
Sweet won the mayor's prize, and Miss Bishop won the popular vote.

120
00:05:47.109 --> 00:05:51.271
Henry thought Maggie might be mad that The Lemonade Detectives hadn't won either prize.

121
00:05:52.371 --> 00:05:53.712
But Maggie didn't mind a bit.

122
00:05:54.336 --> 00:05:57.224
Because The Lemonade Detectives still got interviewed on TV.

123
00:05:59.831 --> 00:06:02.759
They were the kid detectives who'd solved the parade mystery!
